{title: Tere Bin}
{artist: Rabbi Shergill}
{key: D}

{c: Verse 1}
Te [D]re bin sanu sone [G]ya,        Koi [A7]hor naiyyo labh [D]na
Jo [D]deve ruha na sa [G]kun,        Chukke [A7]jo nakhra me [D]ra
Ve me [Bm]sare ghum ke vekhiya,        Am [G]rica rus maleshiya
Na [A]kithe vi koi [Em]fark si,        Har [Em]kise di koi [D]shart si
Koi [Bm]magta mera si sama,        Koi [G]honda surat pe fida
Koi [A]magda meri [Em]si wafa,        Na Koi [Em]mangta meri [D]ya bala
Te [D]re bin hor na ki [G]se,        mag [A7]ni meriya ba [D]la
Te [D]re bin Hor na ki [G]se,        kar [A7]ni dhoop wich [D]chha
Jive [Bm]rukkiya si tu zara,        nahi [G]bhullana main sari umar
Jivein [A]akhiya si akhi [Em]ya chura,        ro [Em]venga sanu [D]yad kar
hasi [Bm]ya si main hasa ajeeb,        par [G]tu nahi si haseeya
Dil [A]wich tere jo [Em]raaz si,        mai [Em]nu tu kyu nahi [D]dasiya
Te [D]re bin sanu eh [G]raz,        kise [A7]hor naiyo das [D]na
Te [D]re bin peed da i [G]laaj,        kis [A7]vaid kolo labh [D]na
Mil [Bm]yasi aaj mainu,        [G]tera ik patra
[A]Likheya si [Em]jeste,        [Em]Sher Vare [D]shah da
[Bm]Padke si osnu,        [G]Hanju ek duliya
[A]Ankhahch [Em]band thi,        te [Em]raaz aaj [D]khuliya
Te [D]re bin aye mere han [G]ju,        kis [A7]nu naiyo chum [D]na
ke Te [D]re bin aye mere han [G]ju,        Mi [A7]tti wich rul [D]na
